 1.  The program takes input of marks multiple students (maximum of 100) using a one-dimensional array.


2.  It calculates the total marks and average the entire class.


3.  It determines the highest scoring student and the lowest scoring student. 


4.  It counts how many students passed and how many failed based on a passing mark condition.


5.  It computes the class average and assigns grade distribution based on the marks obtained.
